## Smalt release VM args (LANE-09, AoQ program brief §4).
##
## +sbt db — scheduler bind type "db": schedulers bind to logical CPU cores
##   in a distribution that keeps AoQ handler processes on fixed cores.
## +sbwt none — no scheduler busy-wait: a scheduler that runs out of work
##   sleeps immediately instead of spinning. Rationale: AoQ handlers are
##   pinned (Smalt.Aoq.Scheduler.pin/1), so busy-wait polling only burns
##   cores the handlers need; latency is dominated by message arrival, not
##   scheduler wakeup.
## +hms 2097152 — default max_heap_size (2_097_152 words = 16 MiB on 64-bit):
##   any process whose heap exceeds the budget is killed (logged). Rationale:
##   AoQ workers additionally carry the same budget via spawn opts
##   (Smalt.Aoq.Worker); the VM-wide default backstops every other process
##   (parsers, listeners, SDK handlers) so a runaway allocation dies instead
##   of degrading the whole node.
+sbt db
+sbwt none
+hms 2097152
